diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index c3f7203..401dfe8 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -8,8 +8,16 @@ The format follows [Keep a Changelog 1.1.0](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/
 
 ### Added
 
+- Optional link expiry: `POST /api/v1/links` accepts `expiresAt` as an RFC 3339 timestamp with an offset; a value at or before now is a 400 field error, a zoneless string is the generic 400 for an unreadable body. Flyway migration `V2__add_link_expiry.sql` adds the nullable `links.expires_at` column; existing rows never expire.
+- `GET` and `HEAD /{code}` answer 410 `/problems/link-expired` with `Cache-Control: no-store` once `expiresAt` has passed; no click is recorded and the redirect counter gains `outcome=expired`. The row and its click history are kept.
+- `expiresAt` (nullable) and `expired` (boolean, computed when the response is built) on `LinkResponse` and `StatsResponse`; metadata and statistics of an expired link stay readable with unchanged counts.
+- Expiry regression suite: `ExpiryIT` with a controllable clock, `ExpiryEdgeCasesTest` fixing the boundary as "expired when `expiresAt <= now`", and `MigrationTest.v2AddsNullableExpiresAt`.
+
 ### Changed
 
+- `LinkAllocator.insert(code, url, now)` became `insert(code, url, now, expiresAt)`; `Link` and `CreateLinkRequest` gained the `expiresAt` component.
+- `ApiExceptionHandler` keeps only the exception-to-problem mapping; body construction and the standardisation of framework-produced bodies moved to the package-private `ProblemResponses` helper. No change in behaviour or in the OpenAPI export.
+
 ### Fixed
 
 ## [0.1.0] - 2026-10-12
